== five groups:        5 monitors, 15 nodes ==
   us-east: primary us-east-a
   us-west: primary us-west-a
   ap-south: primary ap-south-a
   ap-southeast: primary ap-southeast-a
   eu-west: primary eu-west-a
== schema ==
== publications, row-filtered on region ==
== subscriptions: through every node of the publishing group, failover-enabled ==
== waiting for the initial table sync of every subscription ==
== concurrent writers: 2000 rows each, four regions in parallel ==
== settling ==
=== row counts on every primary (expect 8000 everywhere once fully mirrored) ===
us-east: 8000
us-west: 8000
ap-south: 8000
ap-southeast: 8000
eu-west: 8000

=== per-region row counts on the warehouse (expect 2000 each) ===
ap-south: 2000
ap-southeast: 2000
us-east: 2000
us-west: 2000

=== the standbys hold the same rows (physical replication), eu-west and us-east shown ===
eu-west-b: 8000
eu-west-c: 8000
us-east-b: 8000
us-east-c: 8000

=== apply/sync error counts, every primary ===
(pg_stat_subscription_stats' per-conflict-type columns, confl_insert_exists
 and friends, are PG18+; this demo runs PG17, so apply_error_count and
 sync_error_count are what is available.)
-- us-east --
sub_us_east_from_eu_west: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
sub_us_east_from_us_west: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
-- us-west --
sub_us_west_from_us_east: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
-- ap-south --
sub_ap_south_from_ap_southeast: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
sub_ap_south_from_eu_west: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
-- ap-southeast --
sub_ap_southeast_from_ap_south: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
-- eu-west --
sub_eu_west_from_ap_south: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
sub_eu_west_from_us_east: apply_errors=0 sync_errors=0
